<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n27852" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δόκησις</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εως</span>, ἡ, (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δοκέω</span>) <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>opinion, fancy,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δ. δὲ δεῖ λέγειν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hdt.
					7.185
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Chrysipp.Stoic.
				2.22
			</span></i>, etc.; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δ. εἰπεῖν,</span> opp.
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐξακριβῶσαι λόγον,</span>
			<i><span class="en">
				S.
				<u>Tr.</u>
				426
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δ. ἀγνὼς λόγων ἦλθε</span> a
			vague <i>suspicion</i> was thrown out, <i><span class="en">
				Id.
				<u>OT</u>
				681
			</span></i> (lyr.); 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δ. τῆς ἀληθείας</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Th.
					2.35
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δώρων δ.</span>
			<i>suspicion</i> of bribery, <i><span class="en">
				Id.
				5.16
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δ. παρέχειν ὡς</span> . . <i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				<u>Pomp.</u>
				54
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>apparition, phantom,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κενὴν δ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					E.
					<u>Hel.</u>
					36
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σκοπεῖτε μὴ δόκησιν εἴχετ᾽ ἐκ
				θεῶν</span> ib.<i><span class="en">
				119
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οὕτω δοκεῖτε τὴν δ.
			ἀσφαλῆ</span> ib.<i><span class="en">
				121
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>3.</b>
			<i>appearance,</i> opp. reality, <i><span class="en">
				Ph.
				1.222
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φάσμα καὶ δ. ἑαυτῆς παρέχειν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Plu.
					2.392a
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δ. ἰσχίου</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Aret.
					<u>SD</u>
					2.12
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>repute, credit,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Th.
				4.18
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Stoic.</u>
				3.38
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὁ στρατηγὸς τὴν δ. ἄρνυται</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					E.
					<u>Andr.</u>
					696
				</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
